      "writtenOn": "2022-12-06T03:47:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The change is because android hardware health service will register epoll with EPOLLWAKEUP flag [1].  Afterwards, when suspend starts, NETLINK will hold the wakelock because the EPOLLWAKEUP flag registered from health service.\n\nMTK found the problem in Anrdoid T (13?).\nAnd one more key factor is the CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND capability of health service [2] that may affect suspend flow.\n\n[1] https://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/master/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp#69\n[2] https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/1461242\n\nCurrently only the patch referenced in my commit message is available but not accepted in upstream.",
      "parentUuid": "e6353cc7_b02d04e8",
      "revId": "b399bfa3dca9952d2bdf7ea95881df154ada5085",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
